Application and Effect Analysis of Soil Bin Visualization System for Shield Construction in Complex Stratum
MA Runtao1,LI Yongsen2
(1、Guangzhou Metro Group Co.,Ltd. Rail Transit Branch Guangzhou 51330,China; 2、CCCC First Highway Xiamen Engineering Co.,Ltd. Xiamen 361021,China)
Abstract: When shield tunneling in complex strata, how to master the improvement of the residual soil in the silo in real time and judge the stability of the face is always a problem to be solved. This study mainly starts from solving this problem. Under the premise of auxiliary pneumatic tunneling mode, a video surveillance camera is installed on the cone plate at the top of the diaphragm inside the soil bunker and the corresponding mirror washing system is configured. Meanwhile,the video network is directly connected with the shield operating system interface to achieve real-time monitoring of the conditions inside the soil bunker. It can more intuitively monitor the changes of the stratum,the improvement effect of the residue in the soil bin and the wear of the tool,so as to take timely targeted measures,effectively reduce the construction risk and improve the construction efficiency. Key words:complex geology;shield construction;visual system;effect;benefits
